WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.068
-Hi, guys.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:04.737
Welcome to another edition of
"Tonight Show: At Home Edition."

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:08.008
The sun came out just now,
so I figured it's a perfect time

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:11.211
to maybe do the intro
from outside.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.680
We have a great show tonight,
but before we get into the show,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.084
I just do want to say
it's so tough this week.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.385
It's Thursday.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:22.722
And I know everyone's at home,
doing their part,

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.757
staying at home, which is great.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:27.093
I just wanted to give a special
shout-out tonight

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.228
to New York City,
because we do our show

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:30.696
from Manhattan,
in New York City.

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:33.099
And we're very lucky
to do our show from there.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.968
And, so, I just want to say,
New York City,

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:38.604
you're in my thoughts all the
time, but especially today.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:43.409
We're losing
a lot of great people --

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:49.248
transit workers,
sanitation workers,

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:53.285
firefighters, police officers,

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:56.556
people that are just
doing their jobs.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.691
And that's all they're doing.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:03.663
And I just want to let them know
that they will not be forgotten,

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.465
and what they're doing is
an amazing job,

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:07.933
and you make our country proud.

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:09.936
So thank you so much.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:13.939
And just like the sun,
the sun will shine again.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:15.341
It will.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.877
And we'll be back in the city,
doing the show from there.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.012
We have an amazing show tonight.

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:23.816
My favorites of all time, rap
icons, New York City icons --

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:26.419
speaking of New York --
Ad-Rock and Mike D

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.388
from the Beastie Boys
are on the show tonight.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:34.326
And their charity is
foodbanknyc.org.

00:01:34.326 --> 00:01:37.029
Again, thank you,
Winnie, for drawing these.

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:38.865
It kind of looks like
I could have done this one.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.233
Anyway...

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:43.002
But the Beasties have
a story called

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.738
"The Beastie Boys Story"
on Apple TV+ this Friday,

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.139
coming out.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:51.744
Also, we have Anna Kendrick,
whose film, "Trolls World Tour,"

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.246
is out, also on Friday.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.214
And Universal/DreamWorks did
this cool thing where they're

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:57.283
releasing it through TV

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.952
so you don't have to
go to theaters.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.786
I think that's a good move.

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:04.156
Her charity she's working with
is The Trevor Project,

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:10.696
which helps out LGBTQ youth
communities.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:12.832
And you'll see what they do,
the great stuff,

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.667
if you go to that website.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.904
Also, our buddy Sting --
speaking of legends --

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.073
stops by to help me
and The Roots out.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.240
We might have forced him
to do it.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.541
Might have.

00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:26.612
But you'll see what we do with
classroom instruments --

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:28.248
kind of --
just stuff that we can do

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:30.883
around our house with The Roots.

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:32.252
It's an all-new "Tonight Show."

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:36.456
Let's start it with a monologue.
♪♪

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:37.790
Hi, guys.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.358
Welcome to "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:42.328
Well, Passover
started last night,

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.696
and I heard a lot of
people celebrating

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.231
held virtual Seders using Zoom.

00:02:46.231 --> 00:02:48.167
It's great if you ever wanted to
watch your grandpa

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:52.338
eat soup from
the perspective of the spoon.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.772
I saw that Pope Francis will be

00:02:53.772 --> 00:02:56.042
streaming Easter mass
on YouTube.

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.577
You know these
are strange times when

00:02:57.577 --> 00:03:01.680
the pope ends Easter mass with,
"Be sure to like and subscribe.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.083
Smash that like button."

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:07.586
-Wait. Was that number 2?
-Yeah.

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:10.957
It certainly was. Frances?

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.391
That's right --
Easter is in a few days,

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:13.993
but there is an egg shortage.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.728
Did you hear that? Yeah.

00:03:16.728 --> 00:03:18.731
Which means a lot of kids won't
be able to dye eggs.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.667
So if you're a bald dad,
do the right thing --

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.669
let your kids color your head.

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:27.974
♪♪

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.942
Yesterday, Dr. Fauci
said he doesn't think

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:32.011
that we should
ever shake hands again,

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.812
which will be weird when
every job interview

00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:40.086
starts with
an awkward chest bump.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:43.623
Are you pretending
that you're serious again?

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.391
Well, why don't
you just smile and just --

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:48.294
-I am.
-What are you doing?

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.164
That means you're being serious?
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:01.674
What does that mean?
"Sesame Street's"...

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.375
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:06.379
"Sesame Street's" Elmo
is hosting a virtual playdate

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:08.814
to help entertain kids
during the pandemic.

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.349
Meanwhile, the Count
will help parents add up

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:12.518
all the pounds they've gained
during the quarantine.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.921
[ As the Count ]
10, 20, 30 pounds.

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:16.956
Ha ha ha!

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:21.761
You ate too many cookies.
Ha ha ha!

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.896
[ Normal voice ]
I don't know what that is.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:24.964
I don't get it.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.366
I don't really know
what that means.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:29.134
Alright, guys, sit up.
Sit up. Here we go.

00:04:29.134 --> 00:04:31.704
Ready? Some business news.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.173
Disney+ has added more than
50 million subscribers

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.308
in the last five months.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.476
That's incredible.

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:38.210
That's like taking all of
Quibi's subscribers

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:41.880
and adding 50 million.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.249
I saw that Verizon
has now stopped

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.184
all in-home repairs
and installations

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.053
except for emergencies.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.287
Meanwhile, parents were like,

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.389
"I'm stuck with two kids
under 10 and no Internet.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:53.259
This is an emergency."

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.994
Hello!

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:58.030
Hey, put your hand on top of my
hand and say, "Wing-wing."

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.532
-Wing-wing.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:04.570
-Hello?

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.005
-I'm gonna do that.
-Alright.

00:05:07.005 --> 00:05:08.975
-Wing-wing.
-Wing-wing.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:12.178
-Hello?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:14.347
-Can I do that again?
-Yep, you can.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:16.015
Hold on.
Let me tell a joke first.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:18.351
Waffle House is starting to sell
its signature waffle mix

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:20.353
and sold out of it
in four hours.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.388
The first 30 people
who bought it also got

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:26.859
a lipstick-stained mug and
a dried-up syrup container.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.628
And, finally, I saw that April
is National Poetry Month

00:05:29.628 --> 00:05:32.298
or, as parents who
are homeschooling put it,

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:34.033
"Merlot is red,
Bud Light is blue.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.536
Today, mommy and daddy
need juice time, too."

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:39.371
There you go, everybody.
That is our monologue!

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:41.840
It's time for "Hashtags"!

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:47.446
Yay!
-Whoo-hoo!

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:49.114
-Hi, everybody.
It's time for "Hashtags."

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:51.150
We played this game online
where we give you

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:54.820
a subject or a topic and then we
ask you to comment on all those.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:58.257
And, so, our subject was
"my quarantine superpower"

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.425
this week.

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:01.960
We went on Twitter,
and I put an example.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.129
I said,
"I have the superpower --

00:06:04.129 --> 00:06:07.199
I can start an argument
with a single look."

00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:09.134
And, anyways, thank you,
guys, so much for submitting.

00:06:09.134 --> 00:06:12.171
It was number 5 trending,
so thank you so much for that.

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:13.405
I appreciate it.

00:06:13.405 --> 00:06:15.741
So, now I'd like to do this
week's "Hashtags."

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:17.042
You ready?
-Yeah.

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:18.878
-I'll give it to you.
You give it to Franny, okay?

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:23.149
This one is from @PSU-Rose.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.750
She said, "I can tell the
U.S. Mail truck

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.852
from the UPS truck
from the FedEx truck

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:31.623
based only on the sound of their
engines and brakes."

00:06:31.623 --> 00:06:38.798
-What do I do with this?
-You can stack them.

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:41.066
This is from @LizSin35.

00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:42.935
"I can make my face look
like I'm fascinated

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:47.706
when my husband tells the
same story again."

00:06:47.706 --> 00:06:51.710
That got a smile.
Here you go, bud.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:54.480
This one's from @RoamingOceans.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:07:00.887
Said, "Rapid wine-evaporation
capabilities."

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:05.258
This one's from ScottinOhio4Now.

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:07.693
It says, "I can make the numbers
on my scale go up every day."

00:07:07.693 --> 00:07:10.429
Oh, that's a good power.

00:07:10.429 --> 00:07:12.131
There you go.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:23.208
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:23.208 --> 00:07:26.845
-This one is from FedUpHumanKS.

00:07:26.845 --> 00:07:28.080
"Convincing my kid I'm on Zoom

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.784
when I just want to be
alone for a bit."

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:35.320
-Um, Daddy,
why are you sitting on me?

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.689
-Who is saying that?
-Me.

00:07:37.689 --> 00:07:40.526
-Where are you coming from?
-Behind you.

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:44.096
-Are you upstairs?
-Just look behind you!

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:45.898
Right down.
-Are you a flamingo?

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:47.066
-Down!

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:48.901
-Let's just go to
our last hashtag.

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:51.771
This one's from @MaryBarry80.

00:07:51.771 --> 00:07:57.042
She says, "Is rage a
superpower?"

00:07:57.042 --> 00:07:58.210
Those were our "Hashtags."

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.512
Thank you so much for
submitting.

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:00.513
I really appreciate it.

